        "id": "ch15_4-1",
        "text": "Connecting remotely to the Pi\nWhile it\u2019s quite common to see the Raspberry Pi used as a PC in educational settings, it\u2019s more likely\nthat we\u2019ll want to use it as a server of some sort, and therefore connect to it remotely, rather than set\nit up with its own monitor, mouse and keyboard. This is called headless mode, and it\u2019s what we\u2019re\ngoing to look at next.\nConnecting remotely to the Pi\n369\nEsta secci\u00f3n contiene las siguientes subsecciones\n\u2022 Working with a headless Pi\n\u2022 Connecting to the Pi with PowerShell\n\u2022 Connecting to the Pi with VS Code\nSi deseas explorar cualquiera de estas subsecciones, puedes pregunt\u00e1rmelo directamente.",
